**Proposition 4.1 (bounded multiplier at the stated second threshold).**
Under the rank-one hypotheses above, every finite
$t\ge\max(t_0,14400000)$ satisfies

$$
0<\lambda<19200<20000.
\tag{RB.21}
$$

Proof. First, (RB.1) and (RB.5), together with
$u^2+v^2=1$ and $2|uv|\le1$, give the uniform bounds

$$
\begin{aligned}
\|\ell\|_\infty
&\le B_\ell+a_\ell+l_u+l_v
<0.03852<0.04,\\
\|f\|_\infty&\le e+d_*<0.03.
\end{aligned}
\tag{RB.22}
$$

For every feasible common law in the original problem,

$$
0\le J_t\le\int(|\ell|+b_x|f|)\,d\pi
<0.04+0.03\mu<0.4.
\tag{RB.23}
$$

This estimate uses $\int b_x\,d\pi=\mu$ in that same law.

Use the maximum-contrast feasible family of GC.12–GC.13 and
GC.62–GC.64 as a legal comparison for the same moment target.
In its notation $q=\nu/t$, $\nu=\mu/c_f<300$,
$u_R=(1-qu_F)/(1-q)$ and $v_R=(1-qv_F)/(1-q)$.
Its four saturated directions
$(1,\sigma\sqrt{u_F},\upsilon\sqrt{v_F})$ have mass $q/4$,
and its four pure directions
$(1,\sigma\sqrt{u_R},\upsilon\sqrt{v_R})$ have mass $(1-q)/4$,
with $\sigma,\upsilon\in\{\pm1\}$. Coincident directions and zero
pieces at a supplied floor are collected or omitted.

Independent signs cancel all first and mixed live moments and the
mixed failure moment. The live $u^2$ moment is
$q\alpha u_F+(1-q)\alpha u_R=\alpha$. The saturated failure
moments are $qc_f=\mu/t$ and $qc_f\alpha u_F=m_u/t$.
Thus every coordinate of (RB.2) is matched, with legal endpoint
capacity. GC Propositions 12.2 and 10.1 make this a finite original
comparison, not a formal replacement asserted to preserve counts.
Its contrast, the original $r_{\max}(t)$, is

$$
K_{\rm cmp}=r_{\max}(t)
=a\left[q\sqrt{u_F}+\sqrt{(1-q)(1-qu_F)}\right]
\ge a(1-q)>a-\frac{300}{t}.
\tag{RB.24}
$$

Here $0<u_F<1$, $0<q<1$ and $a<1$; no optimal height is
assigned to this comparison.

For any multiplier optimizer of the hypothetical face,
Proposition 3.1 and (RB.24) imply

$$
K_{\rm cmp}-K>\frac1{24000}-\frac{300}{t}
\ge\frac1{48000}\qquad(t\ge14400000).
\tag{RB.25}
$$

Joint attainment in (RB.3) compares the full functional on these
two feasible laws:
$J_t+\lambda K\ge J_{\rm cmp}+\lambda K_{\rm cmp}$.
Since $J_{\rm cmp}\ge0$, (RB.23) yields

$$
\lambda(K_{\rm cmp}-K)\le J_t-J_{\rm cmp}\le J_t<\frac25.
\tag{RB.26}
$$

Dividing by the strict gap in (RB.25) proves
$\lambda<(2/5)48000=19200$. All comparisons retain the original
$\Gamma$, capacity, $K$ and absolute-height problem. $\square$

